<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85626" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέμπω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>conduct, escort,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ὑπ᾽ ἀμύμονι πομπῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.171
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτε θεῶν πομπῇ οὔτε θνητῶν
					ἀνθρώπων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.32
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δόμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.518
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπᾷ Διὸς ξενίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					748
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θείῃ π. χρεώμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.62
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				3.77
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρία π.,</span> of a fair wind,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				352
			</span></i> (troch.); also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνταίαν πνεῦσαι
			π.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1324
			</span></i> (lyr.): in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπολλωνίαις πομπαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					5.91
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεφύροιο πομπαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>N.</u>
					7.29
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλέως ὑπὸ πομπαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					58
				</span></i>
			 (anap.), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			concrete, <i>an escort,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ᾽ εὔφρονι πομπᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					1034
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>sending away, sending home,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπειτα δὲ καὶ περὶ πομπῆς μνησόμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.191
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				8.545
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄφρα τάχιστα πομπῆς καὶ νόστοιο
					τύχῃς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					6.290
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεῦχε δὲ πομπήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.18
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.164
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπᾶς ἁγεμών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					229
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>mission,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῦ τινος πομπῇ</span>
			<i>sent by . . ,</i> of a dream, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.16
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β́,</span> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				383a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ σημείων πομπάς</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				382e
			</span></i>: simply, <i>sending,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξύλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.108
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>solemn procession,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διονύσῳ πομπὴν ἐποιοῦντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heraclit.
					15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ πομπῆς</span>”
				<i>in procession,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.45
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺν πομπῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.197
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπὴν πέμπειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					5.56
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				849
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.56
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς π. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεμπειν</span>, πομπεῦσαι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				4.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1028.14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς π., ὅπως ἂν ὡς κάλλιστα</span>
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεμφθῇ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				12.84.26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> in honour of a god, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				248
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήλων κνισάεσσα πομπά</span>
			the flesh of sheep for sacrifice carried in <i>procession,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				7.80
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> at Rome,
				<i>triumphal procession,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.39.9
			</span></i>, etc.: generally, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τείνειν
			π.</span> lead a long <i>procession,</i> of a military
			expedition, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				613
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>pomp, parade,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. καὶ ῥημάτων ἀγλαϊσμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ax.</u>
					369d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> personified,
			on a vase, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AJA</u>
				30.424
			</span></i>.</div>
